        "content": "// IFL 2016 Paper - Figure 2, 3 & 5\n// Hamming Numbers (Cyclic let):\n// Generates the stream of numbers whose only prime factors are 2, 3, and 5.\n// Demonstrates mutual cyclic let bindings resolved at runtime.\n\n::list = Nil | Cons !x0 x1\n\nstart = el 100 (hamming 1)\n\nmult !a !b = a * b\n\nmap f !xs =\n  case xs\n    (Nil -> Nil)\n    (Cons x xs -> Cons (f x) (map f xs))\n\nel !n !xs =\n  case xs\n    (Nil -> 666)\n    (Cons x xs -> if (n == 0) x (el (n - 1) xs))\n\nmerge !xs !ys =\n  case xs\n    (Nil -> ys)\n    (Cons a as ->\n      case ys\n        (Nil -> xs)\n        (Cons b bs ->\n          if (a == b)\n            (Cons a (merge as bs))\n            (if (a < b)\n              (Cons a (merge as ys))\n              (Cons b (merge xs bs)))))\n\nhamming !n =\n  let h = Cons n (merge (merge as bs) cs),\n      as = map (mult 2) h,\n      bs = map (mult 3) h,\n      cs = map (mult 5) h in\n  h\n"
